            "Because Stephanie's office was devastatingly well-organized, neat, and clean, showing very little sign of neglect, it was unlikely that the previous occupant left the gull behind.",
            "Another possibility was that the gull was a gift, and if it were, Gosling saw no evidence that it reflected an interest in seabirds, since there were no hints at interests in ornithology or animal behavior.",
            "Perhaps the seagull referred to Stephanie's name, whether Seagull, Segal, or Seigel, or Petrel, Gannet, or Albatross, but Gosling knew her last name and there was no seagull connection there.",
            "The emergency gift-buying path, where a panicked shopper hastily bought whatever was closest, was possible but unlikely because a close inspection of the solid screw from which the seagull dangled revealed that Stephanie had made an effort to hang it properly.",
            "Regardless of how it was acquired, the seagull's prominence in the room suggested to Gosling that it served an important psychological purpose and probably elicited a fond memory of a time in her life or an occasion that was meaningful to her.",
            "Stephanie had chosen an elegant mobile whose ponderous movement was calming, rather than a bird made from seashells glued together, a bobbing executive desk ornament with furiously flapping wings, or an enormous bright wall poster of a soaring seabird.",
            "After considering the seagull along with the relaxing CDs on the bookshelf and the absence of highly stimulating decor, Gosling postulated that the bird helped Stephanie regulate her emotions and stay calm, collected, and focused in a difficult and demanding work environment.",
            "Stephanie would not describe the seagull's function in those terms, as she might claim that it makes her feel good or, even more simply, that she just likes it.",
